WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.020
- Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:02.370
I have one more story to share

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:03.570
from the world of social media.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.535
This is "What I'm Liking".

00:00:04.535 --> 00:00:07.020
(upbeat music)
(audience cheering)

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.080
May is Asian-American and
Pacific Islander Heritage Month.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.130
It's a time for celebrating

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:13.950
the rich culture and history
of millions of Americans.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:15.480
A woman in Rhode Island does it

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.910
in her own tiny way, literally.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:20.190
She makes jewelry of
miniature Vietnamese food,

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:21.990
and says it's her way of connecting

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:23.850
with her Vietnamese heritage.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:26.580
So we have some of her jewelry
in studio. It's so cool.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.950
There are dumplings,
spring rolls, bánh mì,

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:31.350
even a bowl of phở. It's incredible.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:33.030
Let's get this very
talented woman in here.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:37.350
Everybody watching on NBC
10 WJAR, say hi to Hana.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:38.183
What's up, Hana?

00:00:38.183 --> 00:00:41.073
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:00:41.073 --> 00:00:41.923
- (laughs) Hi to you.

00:00:41.923 --> 00:00:44.820
- Hello! Your jewelry is so
beautiful and very detailed,

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:47.580
so how hard is that to make?

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.620
- Well, it's definitely a process.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:50.850
Something like the spring rolls,

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.950
they have a transparent
rice paper wrapping,

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:55.260
so I have to use translucent
clay to make them.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.820
Something like the phở has a broth,

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:59.640
so I have to use dyed resin to make that.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:01.440
And so it's a lot of trial and error.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.330
Luckily, I grew up eating Vietnamese food.

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:04.860
My dad is an amazing cook,

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.600
and even though I can't
quite cook like him,

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.068
I'm making miniatures that
look just about the same, so.

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:10.230
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:12.120
- Well, this jewelry is
also meaningful to you,

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:13.710
so can you tell us about that?

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:14.640
- Of course.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.340
So I grew up Vietnamese
in an all-white town,

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.140
and as a non-Vietnamese speaker,

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.850
the best way for me to
connect with my heritage

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.290
was actually through food.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.270
And so what I love about
making these videos

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.520
and sharing the process
is that Vietnamese kids

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:28.087
will come into my comments and say,

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:29.197
"My grandmother makes that,"

00:01:29.197 --> 00:01:30.720
"That's my uncle's favorite dish."

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:31.680
And having that little moment

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:33.870
of connection with them is really special.

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:35.130
- That's super special!
(audience clapping)

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:36.270
Thank you so much, Hana.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:38.880
I love it. It's so cool
and fresh and interesting,

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:40.850
the idea, I'm liking your
post right now, all right?

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:42.300
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:44.040
That's not all, though.
Our season-long partner

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.570
PILOT Pen makers of FriXion,

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:47.490
the go-to erasable pen of
the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:50.010
want to celebrate those
celebrating their heritage

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:50.843
just like you, ma'am.

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:52.680
So they're gonna be writing
you a check for $1,000.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:53.513
How's that sound?

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:55.203
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:01:55.203 --> 00:01:57.879
- Wow, that sounds amazing!

00:01:57.879 --> 00:01:59.943
- Thank you, Hana, for joining us!

00:01:59.943 --> 00:02:02.190
And thank you to all our guests today,

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:05.258
Priyanka Chopra Jonas,
Max and Bouscher Kovsky,

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.410
Emily Crouch, Amy and Dana,

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:08.927
y'all have a great day
(drowned out by audience).

